<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santa María (ship)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1492</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Santa María was the largest of the three ships of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a>'s first voyage in 1492 and served as his flagship. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrack">carrack</a> owned by Juan de la Cosa, it ran aground off the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a> on Christmas Day 1492. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timbers</a> were used to build the fort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-navidad">La Navidad</a>, where Columbus left some 39 men.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santa-maria-ship.jpg" alt="Santa María (ship)" width="320" height="260" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Possibly by Edward H. Hart. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kolumbus-Santa-Maria.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
